From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maago <maago@example.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:23:35 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Open the admin

Bring in the admin: pages where staff list, add, change and delete the
models' rows in the browser. Nothing to write by hand. Two parts:

- The library contrib/admin: routes and pages. main puts
  admin.App(Config) into Config.Apps. Under the prefix /app, it is
  /app/admin/
- The generated admin_gen.go: maago gen writes one for each app with
  models (here board/ and auth/): how the app's models look in the
  admin, the SQL of lists and counts, the forms. It is a *_gen.go, so
  the patch does not have it

Config.Can answers who may do what. It is the copied auth's auth.Can:
nobody who is not staff (a superuser either), everything for a
superuser, and for other staff what their rows of permission
(auth.Permission) allow. It is code of the copy, there to change.

But maago gen refuses:

    board/models.go:12:6: app board has models, but no package uses board.Admin
      fix: add board.Admin to admin.Config.Models in main (D-131), then run maago gen: go build works after gen

Models was given auth.Admin alone. An app with models left out would
have its models vanish from the admin without a word; it is an error
instead. The next commit puts board.Admin in.

Maago-Expect: board/models.go:12:6: app board has models, but no package uses board.Admin

diff --git a/main.go b/main.go
index 159b0ce..805f196 100644
--- a/main.go
+++ b/main.go
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@ import (
 	"os"
 
 	"github.com/maago-web/maago"
+	"github.com/maago-web/maago/contrib/admin"
 	authlib "github.com/maago-web/maago/contrib/auth"
 
 	"example.com/board/auth"
@@ -48,9 +49,12 @@ func main() {
 	// package variables, filled in here.
 	board.Webhook.URL = os.Getenv("BOARD_WEBHOOK_URL")
 	board.Webhook.Token = os.Getenv("BOARD_WEBHOOK_TOKEN")
+	// The admin, at /app/admin/: the models of the apps it is given, to
+	// those auth.Can lets see them.
+	adminApp := admin.App(admin.Config{Models: [][]admin.Model{auth.Admin}, Can: auth.Can})
 	h, err := maago.Handler(maago.Config{
 		DB:   db,
-		Apps: []maago.App{board.App, auth.App},
+		Apps: []maago.App{board.App, auth.App, adminApp},
 		// Who sent the request: the user of its session cookie, or of its
 		// API token. A page that needs one sends the browser to LoginURL.
 		Auth:     auth.Current,
